# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile -- placeholder shipped by the k3s-proxy profile.
#
# A host descriptor with `k3s_proxy_domain = <fqdn>` replaces this file
# at build time (via scripts/lib/host-descriptor.sh) with a real site
# block that terminates TLS and reverse-proxies to the k3s NodePort
# backend. Until then Caddy serves an HTTP-only marker page on port 80
# so the service starts cleanly even without a configured domain.
http://:80 {
	respond "k3s-proxy is up, but no k3s_proxy_domain is configured in the host descriptor yet.\n"
}